reviews.text_weaknesses:
(1) Insufficient explanation of the novelty differences between existing adaptive computing and multi-scale methods;
(2) The key stability indicators during reinforcement learning training were not reported, and the potential impact of high variance in policy gradient estimation in medical image small sample high noise scenarios was not discussed. 
(3) Qualitative or quantitative analysis of failed cases was not provided. For medical applications, it is crucial to understand when a model may incorrectly focus on non lesion areas or excessively contract, resulting in loss of contextual information.

